{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"50058817-5b8d-4005-85b7-b0699d0c6b2b","agentId":"a0c5cf5696591fb76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers. Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no COM3; TestClient + fixture (copy 2026-10-13 lines from C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl at test time; never modify it). Minimal grepping. Report under 100 words. You own cuore/services/system_detail_bridge.py, templates/system.html, static/system.css, mes-log-mcp/mes/electrical.py (additive), mes-log-mcp/mes/faulttree.py NETWORK_CASCADE (additive), cuore/tests/check_system_page.py (extend). Do not touch fullscan*, owner_*, m_*, labels*, scanlog*, liveboard*. You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/) at the end.\n\nThe live network fault: BCM U1713-2F failing now; U1765-86, U1736-87 (BCM), U1736-86/87 (IPC), B10AA-4A, B1040-64 (RFHUB) history since the clear; past sessions showed network codes co-occurring with EVAP 6/18. Build on the electrical/network system page (the 25-key system that holds the bus/network; and the body_comfort page for the BCM): (1) a \"Network event\" section: every U-code across modules from module_dtcs observations with module, failure-type text, status (failing now / history), first/last seen from the car and from MES logs, grouped into one event when ≥3 lost-communication codes share a window (reuse mes.analysis's family logic and wording \"one power or bus event\"); (2) a \"Check first\" checklist generated from mes.electrical for the BCM: battery terminals, BCM supply fuses, BCM grounds (locations from the electrical layout elements already placed; if a ground location is UNKNOWN say so), connector condition, then CAN-C/IHS termination 60 Ω (the sourced test in mechanic_tests) — each row a tickable inspection linking to the inspection form, with the electrical path drawing the page already has; (3) the fault tree for U1713 shows \"-2F signal erratic: intermittent supply/ground or connector before suspecting the bus\" (SAE J2012-DA wording; CORROBORATED for the FTB meaning, the diagnostic order SINGLE-SOURCE from the repo's network cascade); (4) a one-line cross-reference on the EVAP page: \"Network codes have appeared alongside EVAP codes in 6 of 18 sessions on this car; the fuel-level signal reaches the ECM over the bus — see the network event\" (data from the correlation already computed; wording hedged, never cause). Tests: network page shows U1713-2F failing now with \"signal erratic\", the event grouping, the BCM check-first list with ≥5 rows and inspection links; EVAP page shows the cross-reference line. Run check_system_page.py, check_electrical_page.py (if present), check_screens.py. Commit \"Network event view: U-codes across modules, BCM check-first checklist, EVAP cross-reference\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report hash."},"uuid":"0d881b0f-be53-49ca-892c-2e00b68e28ef","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:38:12.885Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
