{"parentUuid":"ffcb2cef-4e85-4260-990f-abed5b4ac44c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"50058817-5b8d-4005-85b7-b0699d0c6b2b","agentId":"a0c5cf5696591fb76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WmFJRkSCiuJqUm3s7jy9ZH","type":"tool_result","content":"53:                 \"lost communication\", \"bus\")"}]},"uuid":"55f738d3-3665-4fbe-8bce-a9877d60616f","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:38:36.636Z","toolUseResult":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"53:                 \"lost communication\", \"bus\")","numLines":1,"totalLines":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ffcb2cef-4e85-4260-990f-abed5b4ac44c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"8ba12dcf-e300-44d0-8305-c3a380ee4095","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"50058817-5b8d-4005-85b7-b0699d0c6b2b","agentId":"a0c5cf5696591fb76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MjmC6RCQTawxYf7eNoYUcy","type":"tool_result","content":"333:NETWORK_CASCADE = Tree(\n334-    key=\"network-cascade\",\n335-    title=\"BCM/RFHUB/DTCM comms cascade (U1711/U1712/U1713/U1716/U2054/\"\n336-          \"U0100/B1040) -- one network event, not seven faults\",\n337-    # U1765 (BCM: lost communication with RF Hub) is named in no document here,\n338-    # but this car logged U1765-86 in SCAN_2609152048 alongside U1711/12/13 --\n339-    # the same lost-communication family, so it takes the same sequence.\n340-    codes=frozenset({\"U1711\", \"U1712\", \"U1713\", \"U1716\", \"U1765\", \"U2054\", \"U0100\",\n341-                      \"B1040\"}),\n342-    framing=(\n343-        \"Every code in this family is a message-integrity failure type -- \"\n344-        \"U-codes by definition, B1040's FTB `64` is 'plausibility' -- not a \"\n345-        \"component-internal fault (GIORGIO_PLATFORM.md section 1's FTB \"\n346-        \"table; mes/analysis.py COMMUNICATION_FTBS).\",\n347-        \"CONNECTIVITY_AND_SGW.md section 1, verbatim: the pervasive U/C \"\n348-        \"lost-communication DTCs -- BCM U1711/U1712/U1713/U1716, DTCM \"\n349-        \"U0100, DASM C1403/C1408/C1431/C141C -- 'name exactly the modules \"\n350-        \"on the unreachable buses'; recommendation there is a key-on-\"\n351-        \"engine-RUNNING rescan before chasing any of them as faults.\",\n352-        \"GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md Table B: whole-vehicle serial UDS sweeps \"\n353-        \"and cable re-plugs manufacture -87/-2F bystander codes -- this \"\n354-        \"car's own SCAN_2609041953 shows exactly that (DTCM U0100-87, BCM \"\n355-        \"U171x-2F, EPS U1960-83). Pull DTC EX before clearing.\",\n356-        \"This repo's own network family rule (mes/knowledge.py match_codes, \"\n357-        \"CORPUS_BASELINE.md section 7.2's proposed reporting rule, mes/\"\n358-        \"analysis.py detect_network_event): three or more modules holding \"\n359-        \"only U/C communication codes with no component-level code of \"\n360-        \"their own collapse into one network-event finding, not N module \"\n361-        \"faults.\",\n362-        \"Ranked, sourced causes on this platform, in the order mes/\"\n363-        \"knowledge.py already uses: BCM supply/fuse F82 (TSB S1808000005), \"\n364-        \"inline connector XY201 + frame grounds G003A/B (TSB S2008000032), \"\n365-        \"then spread/backed-out terminals (TSB S1708000262 REV. A).\",\n366-    ),\n367-    steps=(\n368-        Step(\"N1\", \"Engine-running rescan before chasing any of this as real\",\n369-             \"Rescan with the engine RUNNING (not just key-on-engine-off) \"\n370-             \"and re-read the DTCs fresh.\",\n371-             \"MES full scan, engine running.\",\n372-             \"Codes do not reappear as freshly active with the engine \"\n373-             \"running.\",\n374-             \"Codes persist with the engine running: treat as a real, \"\n375-             \"recurring event and continue down this tree.\",\n376-             \"free / 5 min\",\n377-             \"CONNECTIVITY_AND_SGW.md section 1 -- 'Recommendation: do not \"\n378-             \"chase these as faults without a key-on-engine-RUNNING \"\n379-             \"rescan.'\"),\n380-        Step(\"N2\", \"Pull DTC EX on every code BEFORE clearing anything\",\n381-             \"In MES, read extended DTC data (DTC EX) on every code in \"\n382-             \"this family: odometer, occurrence count, aging counter.\",\n383-             \"MES DTC EX screen.\",\n384-             \"Codes do not all share one identical odometer value and a \"\n385-             \"single occurrence count.\",\n386-             \"Every code shares one odometer value and one occurrence: \"\n387-             \"your own scan (or a cable re-plug) produced them. Clear and \"\n388-             \"move on -- there is nothing to repair. Do this BEFORE \"\n389-             \"clearing; clearing destroys this evidence.\",\n390-             \"free / 5 min\",\n391-             \"GIORGIO_PLATFORM.md section 1 item #3, 'the decisive test, \"\n392-             \"and it is cheap'; GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md Table B ('Pull DTC \"\n393-             \"EX before clearing').\"),\n394-        Step(\"N3\", \"Read ABS directly on CAN-CH (grey A6) -- does the \"\n395-                   \"brake side agree?\",\n396-             \"Fit the grey A6 adapter cable and scan the Continental ABS \"\n397-             \"MK C1 module directly on CAN-CH for its own stored codes.\",\n398-             \"MES + grey A6 cable, CAN-CH bus.\",\n399-             \"ABS reports no fault of its own.\",\n400-             \"ABS itself holds a stored code: the brake side has a \"\n401-             \"genuine finding, and BCM's U1711/U1712 'brake system (NFR) \"\n402-             \"erratic' was reporting on a module that does have a real \"\n403-             \"problem. Diagnose the ABS-reported code itself, outside \"\n404-             \"this tree.\",\n405-             \"needs grey A6 cable / 10 min\",\n406-             \"GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md Table A (ABS Continental MK C1, \"\n407-             \"CAN-CH, grey A6, CONFIRMED) and Table B (CAN-CH bus \"\n408-             \"profile).\",\n409-             caution=\"Listen/scan only -- GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md Table B: \"\n410-                     \"never transmit on CAN-CH without explicit human \"\n411-                     \"confirmation; brakes, airbag squibs and steering \"\n412-                     \"assist live here.\"),\n413-        Step(\"N4\", \"Clear once, then rescan without re-plugging anything\",\n--\n660:TREES: tuple[Tree, ...] = (EVAP_LEAK, P1CEA_FLOW, NETWORK_CASCADE,\n661-                            DASM_HALF_LINK)\n662-\n663-\n664-# --- generic (non-hand-written) trees ---------------------------------------\n665-#\n666-# EVAP was the first code family this project diagnosed, so it got a\n667-# hand-written tree first; the car throws every family SAE defines, and a\n668-# mechanic working, say, a P0301 or a C1234 deserves the same sourced,\n669-# ordered sequence -- built from this repo's own sourced tables instead of\n670-# transcribed by hand. Nothing below is invented: every step cites the\n671-# module (and, through it, the bulletin/part/spec) it came from, and a step\n672-# with no sourced table to draw from is a clearly-marked generic SAE-range\n673-# step, never a guessed one.\n674-\n675-def _sae_generic_steps(base: str) -> list[tuple[str, str, str, str, str, str, str]]:\n676-    \"\"\"Last-resort steps for a code's SAE prefix range, used when (or in\n677-    addition to) the sourced tables above have nothing more specific.\n678-    Each tuple is ``(title, test, tools, expect, if_abnormal, cost,\n679-    source)``; the source always says plainly that this is a generic\n680-    SAE-range convention, not a platform-specific citation.\"\"\"\n681-    if re.match(r\"^P03\\d{2}$\", base):\n682-        return [\n683-            (\"Coil/plug swap test between cylinders\",\n684-             \"Swap the spark plug and ignition coil from the misfiring \"\n685-             \"cylinder with a known-good cylinder's, then recheck which \"\n686-             \"cylinder misfires.\",\n687-             \"Hands.\",\n688-             \"Misfire follows the swapped part to the other cylinder.\",\n689-             \"Misfire follows the part: replace it. Misfire stays on the \"\n690-             \"original cylinder: the cause is mechanical on that cylinder \"\n691-             \"(injector, compression), not the swapped part.\",\n692-             \"cheap / 20 min\",\n693-             \"Generic SAE misfire (P03xx) diagnostic convention -- an \"\n694-             \"industry-standard swap test, not a platform-specific \"\n695-             \"bulletin\"),\n696-            (\"Injector check on the misfiring cylinder\",\n697-             \"Check that cylinder's injector resistance and response to \"\n698-             \"its commanded pulse.\",\n699-             \"Meter; MES live injector parameters if available.\",\n700-             \"Injector in spec and responds to the commanded pulse.\",\n701-             \"Out of spec or unresponsive: replace the injector.\",\n702-             \"meter work / 20 min\",\n703-             \"Generic SAE misfire (P03xx) diagnostic convention\"),\n704-            (\"Compression test on the misfiring cylinder\",\n705-             \"Run a compression (or cylinder-leakage) test on the \"\n706-             \"misfiring cylinder.\",\n707-             \"Compression gauge / leakdown tester.\",\n708-             \"Compression within spec and even across cylinders.\",\n709-             \"Low or uneven compression: a mechanical fault (valve, ring, \"\n710-             \"head) -- no electrical repair will resolve this.\",\n711-             \"shop equipment / 30 min\",\n712-             \"Generic SAE misfire (P03xx) diagnostic convention\"),\n713-        ]\n714-    if re.match(r\"^P017[0-9]$\", base):\n715-        return [\n716-            (\"Vacuum leak smoke/propane test\",\n717-             \"Smoke-test (or propane-sniff) the intake tract for an \"\n718-             \"unmetered air leak.\",\n719-             \"Smoke machine or propane torch.\",\n720-             \"No leak found.\",\n721-             \"Leak found: repair it before suspecting the fuel system.\",\n722-             \"shop equipment / 20 min\",\n723-             \"Generic SAE fuel-trim (P017x) diagnostic convention\"),\n724-            (\"Fuel pressure check\",\n725-             \"Check fuel pressure against the published spec at idle and \"\n726-             \"under load.\",\n727-             \"Fuel pressure gauge / MES live fuel-rail-pressure parameter \"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bdf838b6-2bdf-4f1e-b76b-c742814a0610","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:38:36.729Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"333:NETWORK_CASCADE = Tree(\n334-    key=\"network-cascade\",\n335-    title=\"BCM/RFHUB/DTCM comms cascade (U1711/U1712/U1713/U1716/U2054/\"\n336-          \"U0100/B1040) -- one network event, not seven faults\",\n337-    # U1765 (BCM: lost communication with RF Hub) is named in no document here,\n338-    # but this car logged U1765-86 in SCAN_2609152048 alongside U1711/12/13 --\n339-    # the same lost-communication family, so it takes the same sequence.\n340-    codes=frozenset({\"U1711\", \"U1712\", \"U1713\", \"U1716\", \"U1765\", \"U2054\", \"U0100\",\n341-                      \"B1040\"}),\n342-    framing=(\n343-        \"Every code in this family is a message-integrity failure type -- \"\n344-        \"U-codes by definition, B1040's FTB `64` is 'plausibility' -- not a \"\n345-        \"component-internal fault (GIORGIO_PLATFORM.md section 1's FTB \"\n346-        \"table; mes/analysis.py COMMUNICATION_FTBS).\",\n347-        \"CONNECTIVITY_AND_SGW.md section 1, verbatim: the pervasive U/C \"\n348-        \"lost-communication DTCs -- BCM U1711/U1712/U1713/U1716, DTCM \"\n349-        \"U0100, DASM C1403/C1408/C1431/C141C -- 'name exactly the modules \"\n350-        \"on the unreachable buses'; recommendation there is a key-on-\"\n351-        \"engine-RUNNING rescan before chasing any of them as faults.\",\n352-        \"GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md Table B: whole-vehicle serial UDS sweeps \"\n353-        \"and cable re-plugs manufacture -87/-2F bystander codes -- this \"\n354-        \"car's own SCAN_2609041953 shows exactly that (DTCM U0100-87, BCM \"\n355-        \"U171x-2F, EPS U1960-83). Pull DTC EX before clearing.\",\n356-        \"This repo's own network family rule (mes/knowledge.py match_codes, \"\n357-        \"CORPUS_BASELINE.md section 7.2's proposed reporting rule, mes/\"\n358-        \"analysis.py detect_network_event): three or more modules holding \"\n359-        \"only U/C communication codes with no component-level code of \"\n360-        \"their own collapse into one network-event finding, not N module \"\n361-        \"faults.\",\n362-        \"Ranked, sourced causes on this platform, in the order mes/\"\n363-        \"knowledge.py already uses: BCM supply/fuse F82 (TSB S1808000005), \"\n364-        \"inline connector XY201 + frame grounds G003A/B (TSB S2008000032), \"\n365-        \"then spread/backed-out terminals (TSB S1708000262 REV. A).\",\n366-    ),\n367-    steps=(\n368-        Step(\"N1\", \"Engine-running rescan before chasing any of this as real\",\n369-             \"Rescan with the engine RUNNING (not just key-on-engine-off) \"\n370-             \"and re-read the DTCs fresh.\",\n371-             \"MES full scan, engine running.\",\n372-             \"Codes do not reappear as freshly active with the engine \"\n373-             \"running.\",\n374-             \"Codes persist with the engine running: treat as a real, \"\n375-             \"recurring event and continue down this tree.\",\n376-             \"free / 5 min\",\n377-             \"CONNECTIVITY_AND_SGW.md section 1 -- 'Recommendation: do not \"\n378-             \"chase these as faults without a key-on-engine-RUNNING \"\n379-             \"rescan.'\"),\n380-        Step(\"N2\", \"Pull DTC EX on every code BEFORE clearing anything\",\n381-             \"In MES, read extended DTC data (DTC EX) on every code in \"\n382-             \"this family: odometer, occurrence count, aging counter.\",\n383-             \"MES DTC EX screen.\",\n384-             \"Codes do not all share one identical odometer value and a \"\n385-             \"single occurrence count.\",\n386-             \"Every code shares one odometer value and one occurrence: \"\n387-             \"your own scan (or a cable re-plug) produced them. Clear and \"\n388-             \"move on -- there is nothing to repair. Do this BEFORE \"\n389-             \"clearing; clearing destroys this evidence.\",\n390-             \"free / 5 min\",\n391-             \"GIORGIO_PLATFORM.md section 1 item #3, 'the decisive test, \"\n392-             \"and it is cheap'; GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md Table B ('Pull DTC \"\n393-             \"EX before clearing').\"),\n394-        Step(\"N3\", \"Read ABS directly on CAN-CH (grey A6) -- does the \"\n395-                   \"brake side agree?\",\n396-             \"Fit the grey A6 adapter cable and scan the Continental ABS \"\n397-             \"MK C1 module directly on CAN-CH for its own stored codes.\",\n398-             \"MES + grey A6 cable, CAN-CH bus.\",\n399-             \"ABS reports no fault of its own.\",\n400-             \"ABS itself holds a stored code: the brake side has a \"\n401-             \"genuine finding, and BCM's U1711/U1712 'brake system (NFR) \"\n402-             \"erratic' was reporting on a module that does have a real \"\n403-             \"problem. Diagnose the ABS-reported code itself, outside \"\n404-             \"this tree.\",\n405-             \"needs grey A6 cable / 10 min\",\n406-             \"GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md Table A (ABS Continental MK C1, \"\n407-             \"CAN-CH, grey A6, CONFIRMED) and Table B (CAN-CH bus \"\n408-             \"profile).\",\n409-             caution=\"Listen/scan only -- GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md Table B: \"\n410-                     \"never transmit on CAN-CH without explicit human \"\n411-                     \"confirmation; brakes, airbag squibs and steering \"\n412-                     \"assist live here.\"),\n413-        Step(\"N4\", \"Clear once, then rescan without re-plugging anything\",\n--\n660:TREES: tuple[Tree, ...] = (EVAP_LEAK, P1CEA_FLOW, NETWORK_CASCADE,\n661-                            DASM_HALF_LINK)\n662-\n663-\n664-# --- generic (non-hand-written) trees ---------------------------------------\n665-#\n666-# EVAP was the first code family this project diagnosed, so it got a\n667-# hand-written tree first; the car throws every family SAE defines, and a\n668-# mechanic working, say, a P0301 or a C1234 deserves the same sourced,\n669-# ordered sequence -- built from this repo's own sourced tables instead of\n670-# transcribed by hand. Nothing below is invented: every step cites the\n671-# module (and, through it, the bulletin/part/spec) it came from, and a step\n672-# with no sourced table to draw from is a clearly-marked generic SAE-range\n673-# step, never a guessed one.\n674-\n675-def _sae_generic_steps(base: str) -> list[tuple[str, str, str, str, str, str, str]]:\n676-    \"\"\"Last-resort steps for a code's SAE prefix range, used when (or in\n677-    addition to) the sourced tables above have nothing more specific.\n678-    Each tuple is ``(title, test, tools, expect, if_abnormal, cost,\n679-    source)``; the source always says plainly that this is a generic\n680-    SAE-range convention, not a platform-specific citation.\"\"\"\n681-    if re.match(r\"^P03\\d{2}$\", base):\n682-        return [\n683-            (\"Coil/plug swap test between cylinders\",\n684-             \"Swap the spark plug and ignition coil from the misfiring \"\n685-             \"cylinder with a known-good cylinder's, then recheck which \"\n686-             \"cylinder misfires.\",\n687-             \"Hands.\",\n688-             \"Misfire follows the swapped part to the other cylinder.\",\n689-             \"Misfire follows the part: replace it. Misfire stays on the \"\n690-             \"original cylinder: the cause is mechanical on that cylinder \"\n691-             \"(injector, compression), not the swapped part.\",\n692-             \"cheap / 20 min\",\n693-             \"Generic SAE misfire (P03xx) diagnostic convention -- an \"\n694-             \"industry-standard swap test, not a platform-specific \"\n695-             \"bulletin\"),\n696-            (\"Injector check on the misfiring cylinder\",\n697-             \"Check that cylinder's injector resistance and response to \"\n698-             \"its commanded pulse.\",\n699-             \"Meter; MES live injector parameters if available.\",\n700-             \"Injector in spec and responds to the commanded pulse.\",\n701-             \"Out of spec or unresponsive: replace the injector.\",\n702-             \"meter work / 20 min\",\n703-             \"Generic SAE misfire (P03xx) diagnostic convention\"),\n704-            (\"Compression test on the misfiring cylinder\",\n705-             \"Run a compression (or cylinder-leakage) test on the \"\n706-             \"misfiring cylinder.\",\n707-             \"Compression gauge / leakdown tester.\",\n708-             \"Compression within spec and even across cylinders.\",\n709-             \"Low or uneven compression: a mechanical fault (valve, ring, \"\n710-             \"head) -- no electrical repair will resolve this.\",\n711-             \"shop equipment / 30 min\",\n712-             \"Generic SAE misfire (P03xx) diagnostic convention\"),\n713-        ]\n714-    if re.match(r\"^P017[0-9]$\", base):\n715-        return [\n716-            (\"Vacuum leak smoke/propane test\",\n717-             \"Smoke-test (or propane-sniff) the intake tract for an \"\n718-             \"unmetered air leak.\",\n719-             \"Smoke machine or propane torch.\",\n720-             \"No leak found.\",\n721-             \"Leak found: repair it before suspecting the fuel system.\",\n722-             \"shop equipment / 20 min\",\n723-             \"Generic SAE fuel-trim (P017x) diagnostic convention\"),\n724-            (\"Fuel pressure check\",\n725-             \"Check fuel pressure against the published spec at idle and \"\n726-             \"under load.\",\n727-             \"Fuel pressure gauge / MES live fuel-rail-pressure parameter \"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"dd9a719f-eb5c-41ec-bbd8-f5ed1ebb0294","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"m