{"parentUuid":"4bf474d7-ff70-4cf9-a508-f25b9d9f822f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"50058817-5b8d-4005-85b7-b0699d0c6b2b","agentId":"a0c5cf5696591fb76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018pQEbw6EsT6ELTurpjVat7","type":"tool_result","content":"14-* **A network event is one fault, not five.** When several modules each report\n15-  only \"missing message\" or \"erratic\" against *other* modules, that is one\n16-  power or bus event. Listing five module faults sends a technician chasing\n17:  five repairs. :func:`detect_network_event` collapses them.\n18-\"\"\"\n19-\n20-from __future__ import annotations\n--\n29-\n30-#: Failure-type bytes that mean \"I could not talk to something\", as opposed to\n31-#: \"a component I own is faulty\". Corpus-grounded from MES's own phrasing.\n32:COMMUNICATION_FTBS = {\"2F\", \"86\", \"87\", \"88\", \"64\"}\n33-\n34-#: Minimum distinct modules holding only communication codes before we call it\n35-#: a network event rather than a set of module faults.\n--\n47-    letter = dtc.code[:1].upper()\n48-    if letter == \"U\":\n49-        return True\n50:    if dtc.ftb and dtc.ftb.upper() in COMMUNICATION_FTBS:\n51-        text = f\"{dtc.component} {dtc.description}\".lower()\n52-        hints = (\"communication\", \"can\", \"message\", \"node\", \"module\",\n53-                 \"lost communication\", \"bus\")\n--\n202-        }\n203-\n204-\n205:def detect_network_event(dtcs_by_module: dict[str, list[Dtc]]) -> NetworkEvent | None:\n206-    \"\"\"Collapse a communication-fault cascade into a single finding.\n207-\n208-    A module qualifies only if *every* code it holds is a communication code."}]},"uuid":"9c6848e1-1990-4384-b5b3-2b7228e416a0","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:38:42.094Z","toolUseResult":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"14-* **A network event is one fault, not five.** When several modules each report\n15-  only \"missing message\" or \"erratic\" against *other* modules, that is one\n16-  power or bus event. Listing five module faults sends a technician chasing\n17:  five repairs. :func:`detect_network_event` collapses them.\n18-\"\"\"\n19-\n20-from __future__ import annotations\n--\n29-\n30-#: Failure-type bytes that mean \"I could not talk to something\", as opposed to\n31-#: \"a component I own is faulty\". Corpus-grounded from MES's own phrasing.\n32:COMMUNICATION_FTBS = {\"2F\", \"86\", \"87\", \"88\", \"64\"}\n33-\n34-#: Minimum distinct modules holding only communication codes before we call it\n35-#: a network event rather than a set of module faults.\n--\n47-    letter = dtc.code[:1].upper()\n48-    if letter == \"U\":\n49-        return True\n50:    if dtc.ftb and dtc.ftb.upper() in COMMUNICATION_FTBS:\n51-        text = f\"{dtc.component} {dtc.description}\".lower()\n52-        hints = (\"communication\", \"can\", \"message\", \"node\", \"module\",\n53-                 \"lost communication\", \"bus\")\n--\n202-        }\n203-\n204-\n205:def detect_network_event(dtcs_by_module: dict[str, list[Dtc]]) -> NetworkEvent | None:\n206-    \"\"\"Collapse a communication-fault cascade into a single finding.\n207-\n208-    A module qualifies only if *every* code it holds is a communication code.","numLines":31,"totalLines":31},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4bf474d7-ff70-4cf9-a508-f25b9d9f822f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"483f12cf-7e00-47a9-bc1f-0c2057a8c0ff","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"50058817-5b8d-4005-85b7-b0699d0c6b2b","agentId":"a0c5cf5696591fb76","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LhLYvFhSJLhggPAi2fXbma","type":"tool_result","content":"        Step(\"N4\", \"Clear once, then rescan without re-plugging anything\",\n             \"After N2's DTC EX read, clear the codes, then rescan \"\n             \"without disconnecting or reseating the OBD connector, the \"\n             \"grey/blue adapter, or any bus connector in between.\",\n             \"MES clear + rescan.\",\n             \"Codes stay cleared.\",\n             \"Codes return with nothing re-plugged and no repair \"\n             \"performed: this is a real, recurring network/power event, \"\n             \"not a scan or cable artifact. Proceed to the ranked causes \"\n             \"below.\",\n             \"free / 10 min\",\n             \"CORPUS_BASELINE.md section 7, 2026-08-27 timeline: this \"\n             \"exact sequence on this car went 11:36 SCAN (1 DTC, \"\n             \"U0100-87) -> cleared -> 11:41 SCAN clean across all 8 \"\n             \"modules, with no re-plug in between.\"),\n        Step(\"N5\", \"BCM power feed -- fuse F82 in the rear PDC, BCM A901 \"\n                   \"circuit\",\n             \"Inspect all BCM power feed circuits, including the \"\n             \"standalone 20A fuse and, on this GU/Stelvio, fuse F82 in \"\n             \"the rear PDC feeding the BCM A901 circuit.\",\n             \"Fuse box, meter.\",\n             \"F82 intact; A901 circuit and B+ A0 feed both in spec.\",\n             \"Repair the feed/fuse. A BCM that loses its supply drops off \"\n             \"the bus and every module gatewaying through it throws \"\n             \"U-codes -- matching this car's exact module list.\",\n             \"cheap / 20 min\",\n             \"TSB S1808000005 (2020-04-04), 'No Start, Multiple Modules \"\n             \"Are Not Responding', 2018-2020 Stelvio -- mes/knowledge.py \"\n             \"BULLETINS.\"),\n        Step(\"N6\", \"Inline connector XY201 + frame grounds G003A/G003B\",\n             \"Inspect inline connector XY201 for security; clean and \"\n             \"secure frame grounds G003A and G003B.\",\n             \"Hands / visual, ground cleaning.\",\n             \"Connector fully seated; grounds clean and tight.\",\n             \"Reseat/clean and re-verify (N4) before anything further -- \"\n             \"this is FCA's own published fix for exactly this cascade \"\n             \"shape, no parts required.\",\n             \"free / 20 min\",\n             \"TSB S2008000032 (2020-04-07), 'EVIC Displays Multiple \"\n             \"Warning Messages' -- mes/knowledge.py BULLETINS.\",\n             caution=\"NHTSA associates this bulletin only with 2020 \"\n                     \"Stelvio; GU circuitry is shared but verify \"\n                     \"applicability.\"),\n        Step(\"N7\", \"Spread or backed-out connector terminals\",\n             \"Inspect the involved connector terminals for pushed-out or \"\n             \"spread terminals.\",\n             \"Hands / visual / terminal pick.\",\n             \"Terminals fully seated, no spread pins.\",\n             \"Reseat/repair the terminal and re-verify (N4).\",\n             \"free / 20 min\",\n             \"TSB S1708000262 REV. A (2020-11-17), 'Check Engine Lamp Is \"\n             \"On, Intermittent Module CAN Private Or LIN BUS Codes' -- \"\n             \"mes/knowledge.py BULLETINS.\"),\n        Step(\"N8\", \"BCM water-intrusion recall check (18V205000/U36, \"\n                   \"18V203000/U34)\",\n             \"Pull the passenger kick panel; check the BCM connectors \"\n             \"for staining, a silt line, or green/white corrosion. Check \"\n             \"the cowl drains. Verify whether recalls 18V205000 (U36, \"\n             \"BCM water intrusion) and 18V203000 (U34, liftgate connector \"\n             \"water intrusion) were performed on this VIN.\",\n             \"Hands / visual, VIN recall lookup.\",\n             \"No water staining/corrosion; recall(s) already performed, \"\n             \"sealing kit intact.\",\n             \"Water intrusion found, or the recall was never performed: \"\n             \"corroded BCM connector pins produce faults in both \"\n             \"directions because the BCM gateways CAN-C to CAN-IHS. \"\n             \"Perform/redo the sealing kit -- recurrence after the kit is \"\n             \"documented, so re-verify its integrity even if 'already \"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b5375d0c-79c8-45c9-aa43-49436b0269ee","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:38:42.194Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"        Step(\"N4\", \"Clear once, then rescan without re-plugging anything\",\n             \"After N2's DTC EX read, clear the codes, then rescan \"\n             \"without disconnecting or reseating the OBD connector, the \"\n             \"grey/blue adapter, or any bus connector in between.\",\n             \"MES clear + rescan.\",\n             \"Codes stay cleared.\",\n             \"Codes return with nothing re-plugged and no repair \"\n             \"performed: this is a real, recurring network/power event, \"\n             \"not a scan or cable artifact. Proceed to the ranked causes \"\n             \"below.\",\n             \"free / 10 min\",\n             \"CORPUS_BASELINE.md section 7, 2026-08-27 timeline: this \"\n             \"exact sequence on this car went 11:36 SCAN (1 DTC, \"\n             \"U0100-87) -> cleared -> 11:41 SCAN clean across all 8 \"\n             \"modules, with no re-plug in between.\"),\n        Step(\"N5\", \"BCM power feed -- fuse F82 in the rear PDC, BCM A901 \"\n                   \"circuit\",\n             \"Inspect all BCM power feed circuits, including the \"\n             \"standalone 20A fuse and, on this GU/Stelvio, fuse F82 in \"\n             \"the rear PDC feeding the BCM A901 circuit.\",\n             \"Fuse box, meter.\",\n             \"F82 intact; A901 circuit and B+ A0 feed both in spec.\",\n             \"Repair the feed/fuse. A BCM that loses its supply drops off \"\n             \"the bus and every module gatewaying through it throws \"\n             \"U-codes -- matching this car's exact module list.\",\n             \"cheap / 20 min\",\n             \"TSB S1808000005 (2020-04-04), 'No Start, Multiple Modules \"\n             \"Are Not Responding', 2018-2020 Stelvio -- mes/knowledge.py \"\n             \"BULLETINS.\"),\n        Step(\"N6\", \"Inline connector XY201 + frame grounds G003A/G003B\",\n             \"Inspect inline connector XY201 for security; clean and \"\n             \"secure frame grounds G003A and G003B.\",\n             \"Hands / visual, ground cleaning.\",\n             \"Connector fully seated; grounds clean and tight.\",\n             \"Reseat/clean and re-verify (N4) before anything further -- \"\n             \"this is FCA's own published fix for exactly this cascade \"\n             \"shape, no parts required.\",\n             \"free / 20 min\",\n             \"TSB S2008000032 (2020-04-07), 'EVIC Displays Multiple \"\n             \"Warning Messages' -- mes/knowledge.py BULLETINS.\",\n             caution=\"NHTSA associates this bulletin only with 2020 \"\n                     \"Stelvio; GU circuitry is shared but verify \"\n                     \"applicability.\"),\n        Step(\"N7\", \"Spread or backed-out connector terminals\",\n             \"Inspect the involved connector terminals for pushed-out or \"\n             \"spread terminals.\",\n             \"Hands / visual / terminal pick.\",\n             \"Terminals fully seated, no spread pins.\",\n             \"Reseat/repair the terminal and re-verify (N4).\",\n             \"free / 20 min\",\n             \"TSB S1708000262 REV. A (2020-11-17), 'Check Engine Lamp Is \"\n             \"On, Intermittent Module CAN Private Or LIN BUS Codes' -- \"\n             \"mes/knowledge.py BULLETINS.\"),\n        Step(\"N8\", \"BCM water-intrusion recall check (18V205000/U36, \"\n                   \"18V203000/U34)\",\n             \"Pull the passenger kick panel; check the BCM connectors \"\n             \"for staining, a silt line, or green/white corrosion. Check \"\n             \"the cowl drains. Verify whether recalls 18V205000 (U36, \"\n             \"BCM water intrusion) and 18V203000 (U34, liftgate connector \"\n             \"water intrusion) were performed on this VIN.\",\n             \"Hands / visual, VIN recall lookup.\",\n             \"No water staining/corrosion; recall(s) already performed, \"\n             \"sealing kit intact.\",\n             \"Water intrusion found, or the recall was never performed: \"\n             \"corroded BCM connector pins produce faults in both \"\n             \"directions because the BCM gateways CAN-C to CAN-IHS. \"\n             \"Perform/redo the sealing kit -- recurrence after the kit is \"\n             \"documented, so re-verify its integrity even if 'already \"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"03fdeb1b-8422-40e3-9318-e54da216a03f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"483f12cf-7e00-47a9-bc1f-0c2057a8c0ff","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
